IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting (Class Licence) (Amendment) Notification 2003 (S 555/2003), made under ss 9 and 11 of the Act.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-class-licence-amendment-notification-2003/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-S555-2003.txt (e-Gazette PDF, pdftotext -layout, unedited). Quotations below are lines of THAT file; `srcrefs.py` is run on this module against it.
-- First published 28 November 2003 at 5:00 pm; "shall come into operation on 1st December 2003" (paragraph 1).
-- It amends paragraph 2 of N 1 and the Schedule (paragraphs 1 and 9 amended, paragraph 9A new). The Schedule is not in the lawplain text of N 1.

§ `Paragraphs 1 to 3`

-- src:3 | First published in the Government Gazette, Electronic Edition, on 28th November 2003 at 5:00 pm.
-- src:20 | 1. This Notification may be cited as the Broadcasting (Class
-- src:21 | Licence) (Amendment) Notification 2003 and shall come into
-- src:22 | operation on 1st December 2003.
@ref S 555/2003 publication line and para 1 (commencement) (src:3-22)
GIVEN `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 555/2003 the amendments are in operation on` MEANS
    `the day of the conduct` AT LEAST (Date 1 12 2003)

-- src:25 | 2. Paragraph 2 of the Broadcasting (Class Licence) Notification
-- src:26 | (N 1) is amended —
-- src:27 | (a) by deleting the words ‘‘section 26 of the Telecommunication
-- src:28 | Authority of Singapore Act (Cap. 323)’’ in paragraph (a)
-- src:29 | of the definition of ‘‘Internet Service Provider’’ and
-- src:30 | substituting the words ‘‘section 5 of the Telecommunications
-- src:31 | Act (Cap. 323)’’; and
-- src:32 | (b) by deleting the words ‘‘section 26 of the Telecommunication
-- src:33 | Authority of Singapore Act (Cap. 323)’’ in the definition of
-- src:34 | ‘‘VAN computer on-line service’’ and substituting the words
-- src:35 | ‘‘section 5 of the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)’’.
-- src:38 | 3. The Schedule to the Broadcasting (Class Licence) Notification is
-- src:39 | amended —
-- src:40 | (a) by deleting the words ‘‘section 21’’ in the definitions of
-- src:41 | ‘‘licensee’’ and ‘‘service’’ in paragraph 1 and substituting in
-- src:42 | each case the words ‘‘section 9’’; and
@ref S 555/2003 paras 2 and 3(a): cross-references corrected ("section 26 of the Telecommunication Authority of Singapore Act" becomes "section 5 of the Telecommunications Act"; "section 21" becomes "section 9") (src:25-42)
-- Reference corrections only; no rule.

-- src:45 | (b) by deleting paragraph 9 and substituting the following
-- src:46 | paragraphs:
-- src:47 | ‘‘9.—(1) A licensee who intends to broadcast its service on —
-- src:48 | (a) a radio frequency;
-- src:49 | (b) any spare capacity or sub-carrier on a television or radio
-- src:50 | channel; or
-- src:51 | (c) television lines in the Vertical Blanking Interval,
-- src:52 | shall, before the commencement of the broadcast of its service, apply
-- src:53 | to the Authority for approval to broadcast its service by such means.
-- src:54 | (2) A licensee shall comply with the conditions attached to any
-- src:55 | approval issued by the Authority under sub-paragraph (1), which may
-- src:56 | include the condition requiring the payment of spectrum utilisation
-- src:57 | fees.
@ref S 555/2003 para 3(b): Schedule para 9 substituted (approval to broadcast on a radio frequency, spare capacity or sub-carrier, or Vertical Blanking Interval lines) (src:45-57)
GIVEN `the licensee intends to broadcast its service on a radio frequency, on spare capacity or a sub-carrier on a television or radio channel, or on television lines in the Vertical Blanking Interval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee applied to the Authority for approval before the broadcast began` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 555/2003 N 1 Schedule para 9(1) the licensee has complied` MEANS
    (NOT `the licensee intends to broadcast its service on a radio frequency, on spare capacity or a sub-carrier on a television or radio channel, or on television lines in the Vertical Blanking Interval`) OR `the licensee applied to the Authority for approval before the broadcast began`

GIVEN `the licensee complies with the conditions attached to the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 555/2003 N 1 Schedule para 9(2) the licensee has complied` MEANS
    `the licensee complies with the conditions attached to the approval`

-- src:59 | 9A. A licensee who provides a teletext service after 1st December
-- src:60 | 2003 shall pay an annual licence fee of $2,000 for each period of
-- src:61 | 12 months commencing from —
-- src:62 | (a) that date if the licensee starts to provide, or is continuing to
-- src:63 | provide a teletext service it is already providing on that date;
-- src:64 | or
-- src:65 | (b) the date the licensee starts providing its teletext service.’’.
@ref S 555/2003 para 3(b): Schedule para 9A (annual licence fee of $2,000 for a teletext service) (src:59-65)
GIVEN `the licensee provides a teletext service after 1 December 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`S 555/2003 N 1 Schedule para 9A the annual licence fee for each period of 12 months` MEANS
    IF `the licensee provides a teletext service after 1 December 2003` THEN 2000 ELSE 0
